2:T6d3,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does kitchen fitting labour cost in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There is no single labour price for kitchen fitting. The final cost depends on the kitchen size and layout, preparation work, services, materials and finishing tasks. Every project is different, so obtain a written scope and a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to pay a kitchen fitter by the day?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not necessarily. A day rate can suit flexible or uncertain work, but a fixed quote may provide better budget control when the scope is clear. Compare the total expected cost, not just the daily figure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is included in a kitchen fitting quote?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It may include cabinet installation, worktops, appliances and basic connections, while plumbing, electrics, tiling, flooring, removal and waste disposal may be priced separately. Check the written scope carefully."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I get more than one kitchen fitting estimate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Comparing more than one detailed estimate can help identify missing tasks and different assumptions. Make sure each fitter is pricing the same layout, materials and specification."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I avoid unexpected kitchen fitting costs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Agree the layout and specification in writing, ask about exclusions, confirm how variations are priced and allow a contingency for hidden damage, uneven surfaces or outdated services."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-fitting-price-work","d"]
